# BPMS Database Schema

## 1. roles

### Purpose

Stores the roles available in the BPMS.

### Columns

| Column | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| id | BIGINT | PRIMARY KEY, AUTO_INCREMENT | Unique role identifier |
| name | VARCHAR(50) | NOT NULL, UNIQUE | Name of the role |

### Initial Roles

- ADMIN
- MANAGER
- HR
- EMPLOYEE


## 2. users

### Purpose

Stores the users who interact with the BPMS.

### Columns

| Column | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| id | BIGINT | PRIMARY KEY, AUTO_INCREMENT | Unique user identifier |
| name | VARCHAR(100) | NOT NULL | User's full name |
| email | VARCHAR(150) | NOT NULL, UNIQUE | User's login/contact email |
| password | VARCHAR(255) | NOT NULL | Hashed user password |
| role_id | BIGINT | NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY | Role assigned to the user |
| created_at | TIMESTAMP | NOT NULL | User creation time |
| updated_at | TIMESTAMP | NOT NULL | Last update time |

### Foreign Key

`users.role_id` references `roles.id`.

### Relationship

- One role can have many users.
- Many users can have one role.

```text
roles
  1
  |
  |
  N
users
````

## 3. processes

### Purpose

Stores the business processes or workflows managed by the BPMS.

### Columns

| Column      | Data Type    | Constraints                 | Description                  |
| ----------- | ------------ | --------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| id          | BIGINT       | PRIMARY KEY, AUTO_INCREMENT | Unique process identifier    |
| name        | VARCHAR(150) | NOT NULL                    | Name of the business process |
| description | TEXT         | NULL                        | Description of the process   |
| created_by  | BIGINT       | NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY       | User who created the process |
| created_at  | TIMESTAMP    | NOT NULL                    | Process creation time        |
| updated_at  | TIMESTAMP    | NOT NULL                    | Last update time             |

### Foreign Key

`processes.created_by` references `users.id`.

### Relationship

* One user can create many processes.
* Each process is created by one user.

```text
users
  1
  |
  |
  N
processes
```

## 4. tasks

### Purpose

Stores the individual tasks that belong to a business process.

### Columns

| Column      | Data Type    | Constraints                 | Description                       |
| ----------- | ------------ | --------------------------- | --------------------------------- |
| id          | BIGINT       | PRIMARY KEY, AUTO_INCREMENT | Unique task identifier            |
| process_id  | BIGINT       | NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY       | Process to which the task belongs |
| name        | VARCHAR(150) | NOT NULL                    | Name of the task                  |
| description | TEXT         | NULL                        | Description of the task           |
| status      | VARCHAR(30)  | NOT NULL                    | Current status of the task        |
| assigned_to | BIGINT       | NULL, FOREIGN KEY           | User responsible for the task     |
| created_at  | TIMESTAMP    | NOT NULL                    | Task creation time                |
| updated_at  | TIMESTAMP    | NOT NULL                    | Last update time                  |

### Foreign Keys

* `tasks.process_id` references `processes.id`.
* `tasks.assigned_to` references `users.id`.

### Relationships

* One process can have many tasks.
* Each task belongs to one process.
* One user can be assigned many tasks.
* A task can be unassigned.

```text
processes
    1
    |
    |
    N
  tasks
```

```text
users
  1
  |
  |
  N
tasks
```

## Task Status Values

The task status can have the following values:

* PENDING
* IN_PROGRESS
* COMPLETED
* CANCELLED

