# Relationships Summary

| Parent Table | Child Table | Relationship | Foreign Key |
|---|---|---|---|
| roles | users | One-to-Many | users.role_id |
| users | processes | One-to-Many | processes.created_by |
| processes | tasks | One-to-Many | tasks.process_id |
| users | tasks | One-to-Many | tasks.assigned_to |
```

**This is the version you can keep as your `database-schema.md` documentation.**

## 3. processes

### Purpose

Stores the business workflows managed by the BPMS.

### Columns

| Column | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| id | BIGINT | PRIMARY KEY | Unique identifier for the process |
| name | VARCHAR(150) | NOT NULL, UNIQUE | Name of the business process |
| description | VARCHAR(500) | NULL | Description of the process |
| status | VARCHAR(30) | NOT NULL | Current status of the process |
| created_at | TIMESTAMP | NOT NULL | Process creation time |
| updated_at | TIMESTAMP | NOT NULL | Last update time |

### Initial Status Values

- ACTIVE
- INACTIVE


Process: Employee Leave Request

        ┌──────────────────────────┐
Step 1  │ Manager Approval         │
        └────────────┬─────────────┘
                     ↓
        ┌──────────────────────────┐
Step 2  │ HR Verification           │
        └────────────┬─────────────┘
                     ↓
        ┌──────────────────────────┐
Step 3  │ Complete                 │
        └──────────────────────────┘


## 4. process_steps

### Purpose

Stores the individual stages of a business process and defines the order in which they should be executed.

### Columns

| Column | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| id | BIGINT | PRIMARY KEY | Unique identifier for the process step |
| process_id | BIGINT | NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY | Process to which the step belongs |
| step_name | VARCHAR(150) | NOT NULL | Name of the workflow step |
| step_order | INT | NOT NULL | Defines the execution order |
| required_role | VARCHAR(50) | NOT NULL | Role responsible for handling the step |

### Relationship

- One process can contain many process steps.
- `process_steps.process_id` references `processes.id`.

```text
processes
    1
    |
    | N
    ▼
process_steps


## 5. tasks

### Purpose

Stores the actual work items generated from process steps and assigned to users for execution.

### Columns

| Column | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| id | BIGINT | PRIMARY KEY | Unique identifier for the task |
| process_id | BIGINT | NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY | Process associated with the task |
| process_step_id | BIGINT | NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY | Current process step |
| assigned_to | BIGINT | NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY | User responsible for the task |
| status | VARCHAR(30) | NOT NULL | Current status of the task |
| created_at | TIMESTAMP | NOT NULL | Task creation time |
| updated_at | TIMESTAMP | NOT NULL | Last update time |

### Relationships

- Many tasks can belong to one process.
- Many tasks can belong to one process step.
- Many tasks can be assigned to one user.

```text
processes
    1
    |
    | N
    ▼
  tasks

process_steps
    1
    |
    | N
    ▼
  tasks

users
    1
    |
    | N
    ▼
  tasks

## 6. approvals

### Purpose

Stores the decisions made by users while processing tasks.

### Columns

| Column | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| id | BIGINT | PRIMARY KEY | Unique identifier for the approval |
| task_id | BIGINT | NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY | Task associated with the approval |
| approved_by | BIGINT | NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY | User who made the decision |
| decision | VARCHAR(30) | NOT NULL | Decision made on the task |
| comment | VARCHAR(500) | NULL | Optional comment explaining the decision |
| created_at | TIMESTAMP | NOT NULL | Time when the decision was recorded |

### Relationships

- One task can have multiple approval/action records.
- One user can make many approval decisions.
- `approvals.task_id` references `tasks.id`.
- `approvals.approved_by` references `users.id`.

```text
tasks
  1
  |
  | N
  ▼
approvals

users
  1
  |
  | N
  ▼
approvals

## 7. notifications

### Purpose

Stores notifications that are generated for users when important events occur in the BPMS.

### Columns

| Column | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| id | BIGINT | PRIMARY KEY | Unique identifier for the notification |
| user_id | BIGINT | NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY | User who receives the notification |
| message | VARCHAR(500) | NOT NULL | Notification message |
| is_read | BOOLEAN | NOT NULL | Indicates whether the notification has been read |
| created_at | TIMESTAMP | NOT NULL | Time when the notification was created |

### Relationship

- One user can receive many notifications.
- `notifications.user_id` references `users.id`.

```text
users
  1
  |
  | N
  ▼
notifications

## 8. audit_logs

### Purpose

Stores a record of important actions performed by users in the BPMS for tracking and auditing purposes.

### Columns

| Column | Data Type | Constraints | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| id | BIGINT | PRIMARY KEY | Unique identifier for the audit log |
| user_id | BIGINT | NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY | User who performed the action |
| action | VARCHAR(100) | NOT NULL | Action performed |
| entity_type | VARCHAR(50) | NOT NULL | Type of entity affected |
| entity_id | BIGINT | NOT NULL | ID of the affected entity |
| created_at | TIMESTAMP | NOT NULL | Time when the action occurred |

### Relationship

- One user can generate many audit log records.
- `audit_logs.user_id` references `users.id`.

```text
users
  1
  |
  | N
  ▼
audit_logs

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CREATE TABLE roles (
  id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
  name VARCHAR(50) UNIQUE NOT NULL
);

CREATE TABLE users (
  id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
  name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
  email VARCHAR(150) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
  password VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
  role_id BIGINT NOT NULL,
  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  FOREIGN KEY (role_id) REFERENCES roles(id)
);

CREATE TABLE processes (
  id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
  name VARCHAR(150) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
  description VARCHAR(500),
  status VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'ACTIVE',
  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

CREATE TABLE process_steps (
  id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
  process_id BIGINT NOT NULL,
  step_name VARCHAR(150) NOT NULL,
  step_order INT NOT NULL,
  required_role VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
  FOREIGN KEY (process_id) REFERENCES processes(id)
);

-- THIS IS THE MISSING TABLE - ADD THIS
CREATE TABLE process_instances (
  id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
  process_id BIGINT NOT NULL,
  started_by BIGINT NOT NULL,
  current_step_id BIGINT,
  status VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'RUNNING',
  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  FOREIGN KEY (process_id) REFERENCES processes(id),
  FOREIGN KEY (started_by) REFERENCES users(id)
);

CREATE TABLE tasks (
  id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
  process_instance_id BIGINT NOT NULL,
  process_step_id BIGINT NOT NULL,
  assigned_to BIGINT NOT NULL,
  status VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'PENDING',
  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  FOREIGN KEY (process_instance_id) REFERENCES process_instances(id),
  FOREIGN KEY (process_step_id) REFERENCES process_steps(id),
  FOREIGN KEY (assigned_to) REFERENCES users(id)
);

CREATE TABLE approvals (
  id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
  task_id BIGINT NOT NULL,
  approved_by BIGINT NOT NULL,
  decision VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL, -- APPROVED / REJECTED
  comment VARCHAR(500),
  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  FOREIGN KEY (task_id) REFERENCES tasks(id),
  FOREIGN KEY (approved_by) REFERENCES users(id)
);

CREATE TABLE audit_logs (
  id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
  user_id BIGINT NOT NULL,
  action VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
  entity_type VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
  entity_id BIGINT NOT NULL,
  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users(id)
);
-- notifications table you can add later, not needed for MVP

 @Id
    private int id;
    private String name;